                                "target_word": "martyr",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fbf299e-768b-320a-93b5-73210fd31785",
                                        "entry_id": "369f21c4-3b29-3a97-b03f-59b5a77a7b2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make someone into a martyr by putting them to death for adhering to, or acting in accordance with, some belief, especially religious; to sacrifice on account of faith or profession."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f63062c-1ed2-4cb0-9479-519cec85a9ff",
                                                "sense_id": "6fbf299e-768b-320a-93b5-73210fd31785",
                                                "text": "Fr. Felipe Císcar Puig was a Valencian priest who is also also considered a martyr of the sacramental seal because he was martyred after keeping confessions secret during the religious persecution of the Spanish Civil War."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13e32090-79e1-3cc6-aa60-d02f640cfa86",
                                        "entry_id": "369f21c4-3b29-3a97-b03f-59b5a77a7b2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To persecute."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de788642-0a53-4334-9ba5-f24e95ce96ce",
                                                "sense_id": "13e32090-79e1-3cc6-aa60-d02f640cfa86",
                                                "text": "Some religious and other minorities were martyred until extinction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5717d38e-7aa2-354e-856f-791ec838452f",
                                        "entry_id": "369f21c4-3b29-3a97-b03f-59b5a77a7b2d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To torment; to torture."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d50be658-2a74-4922-81f8-a362ebbf94c9",
                                                "sense_id": "5717d38e-7aa2-354e-856f-791ec838452f",
                                                "text": "Hark, wretches, how I mean to martyr you.\nThis one hand yet is left to cut your throats,\nWhiles that Lavinia ’tween her stumps doth hold\nThe basin that receives your guilty blood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e685b67-a703-4eaa-8968-726afd84c46c",
                                                "sense_id": "5717d38e-7aa2-354e-856f-791ec838452f",
                                                "text": "[…]The louely Amoret, whoſe gentle hart\nThou martyreſt with ſorow and with ſmart,[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
